// The frame-budget reference scene (RFC-0032 §R7, RFC-0033 §G5, INV-21).
//
// ── Do not edit this file casually ────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Every ceiling in `tests/frame_budget.rs` was recorded against *this* scene.
// Changing what it renders changes what those numbers mean, so an edit here is
// an edit to the budget: it needs the same justification a raised ceiling
// needs, in the same place (the PR description), and the recorded numbers must
// be re-taken in the same commit.
//
// ── What it has to contain, and why ───────────────────────────────────────
//
// The scene exists to make one frame's cost measurable, so it holds one of
// everything the per-frame path can be made to do wrong:
//
//   • a value-driven colour   — a paint-only change, which must produce a
//                               scissored redraw and *no* layout work at all;
//   • a value-driven height   — a layout-affecting change, which must reflow
//                               the siblings below it without marking them;
//   • wrapping paragraphs     — the text measure protocol, and the leaves that
//                               must never be re-shaped while their content is
//                               unchanged. Four of them, because one would let
//                               a per-leaf regression hide inside the noise;
//   • a `Canvas`             — the analytic-SDF pipeline, so the arena serves
//                               more than one instance format;
//   • a `for` loop           — so the pool machinery is exercised and a
//                               structural-reconcile regression shows up as a
//                               rebuild rather than as nothing.
//
// It deliberately does **not** animate. The budget is about what a frame costs
// when the app is idle and one value moves — that is the case a real app
// spends its life in, and the case every one of these ceilings was inert for.
View Budget() {
    var hot = false
    var tall = false

    let rows = ["one", "two", "three", "four"]

    Column #[bg: 0x101014, p: 16, gap: 10, width: 640, height: 480] {
        Text("frame budget reference scene") #[color: 0xFFFFFF, size: 20, weight: bold]

        // Paint-only: colour is not a layout input.
        Box #[width: 120, height: 40, radius: 8, bg: hot ? 0xFF3366 : 0x3366FF] {}

        // Layout-affecting: everything below reflows, and nothing below is
        // marked by anyone.
        Box #[width: 120, height: tall ? 90 : 30, radius: 8, bg: 0x22CC88] {}

        Canvas #[width: 60, height: 60] {
            arc(cx: 30, cy: 30, r: 22, stroke: 0x6750A4, stroke_width: 5, cap: round)
        }

        for r in rows {
            Text("Paragraph {r}: a wrapping run of text that is measured inside layout and shaped inside the encoder, and that must be skipped by both once it has been laid out and drawn one time.")
                #[color: 0x9AA0AC, size: 13]
        }
    }
}
